class:: LoziMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Lozi map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/HenonMap

description::

The Lozi map acts as a piecewise-linear simplification of the Hénon map. By replacing the smooth quadratic fold with an absolute value function, the underlying strange attractor loses its curves and becomes sharp and angular. Conceptually, this preserves the bounded chaotic sequences of the Hénon map but replaces smooth transitions with sudden linear zig-zags. This provides sharp, sudden jumps and angular control signals, highly effective for aggressive IDM-style sequencing or percussive parameter automation.

Implements René Lozi's piecewise-linear Hénon-like recurrence code::x' = 1 - a*abs(x) + b*y:: and code::y' = x::. Parameters are sampled at each trigger and are not clipped.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, LoziMap holds between events; unlike Stepper, it exposes a two-state piecewise nonlinear system.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::lozi-map-phase.png#The default Lozi attractor after its transient. x is horizontal and y is vertical; its angular folds reflect the map's absolute-value nonlinearity.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: a
Absolute-value coefficient.
argument:: b
Old-y coupling coefficient.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate.
argument:: reset
Restore initial coordinates on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ LoziMap.ar(Impulse.ar(500))[0] * 0.08 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(LoziMap.kr(Impulse.kr(20))[0].linexp(-2, 2, 80, 2400), 0, 0.08) }.play
)
::

code::
// Angular IDM Bass Sequences
(
{
    var trig, coords, freq, sig, env;
    trig = Impulse.kr(6);
    coords = LoziMap.kr(trig);
    // The sharp, piecewise-linear chaos provides jagged, aggressive jumps
    freq = coords[0].linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 40, 200);
    sig = LPF.ar(Saw.ar(freq), coords[1].linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 100, 3000));
    env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 0.15), trig);
    Pan2.ar(sig * env * 0.5, coords[0])
}.play;
)
::




subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Lozi map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-1.5, 1.5], [-1.5, 1.5],
    { LoziMap.kr(Impulse.kr(100)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-1.5, 1.5).linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-1.5, 1.5).linlin(-1.5, 1.5, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::
